---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AffiliateLink from "../../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Animal Crossing: New Horizons — Still Worth Buying?"
  description="A buying guide for Animal Crossing: New Horizons on Switch: what's in the game, the Happy Home Paradise DLC, and where to buy cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Animal Crossing: New Horizons — Still Worth Buying?</h1>
    <p class="meta">Nintendo Switch · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Animal Crossing: New Horizons</strong> is the cozy life-sim that
      defined the early Switch era. You build up an island, befriend villagers, and
      play at your own pace — there's no fail state and no pressure.
    </p>

    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An open-ended island you terraform, decorate, and populate</li>
      <li>Seasonal events that track the real-world calendar</li>
      <li>Local and online multiplayer (visit friends' islands)</li>
      <li>The <em>Happy Home Paradise</em> DLC for home-design gameplay</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>
      Perfect for relaxed players, families, and anyone who wants a game that fits
      around a busy life rather than demanding hours at a time. Less so for players
      who need goals, combat, or a clear ending.
    </p>

    <h2>Should you buy the DLC?</h2>
    <p>
      Happy Home Paradise is available via the Nintendo Switch Online + Expansion
      Pack subscription, so if you already subscribe, you already own it. Buying it
      standalone only makes sense if you don't want the subscription.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to buy cheapest</h2>
    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Animal+Crossing+New+Horizons+Switch"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post { padding: 1.5rem 0; max-width: 720px; }
  .post h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .buy-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
